# Agency Compatibility Preview Release

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Public unsigned Windows11 x64 v0.2.0-preview.3 / Windows0.2.0.3
Dependencies: 58_INSTALLER_RELEASE.todo, 62_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_RELEASE.todo, 63_AGENCY_VERSION_COMPATIBILITY.todo

## Purpose

Publish the completed disabled-Ask repair and backward/forward runtime-contract compatibility
through the existing unsigned preview channel. The owner requested publication on October11
at20:29. This is not a claim that every device, capture backend or future provider is qualified.

## Tasks

- [x] Confirm publication request and existing repository-scoped publishing access.
- [x] Update candidate version, current guides, website links and reviewed source annotations.
- [ ] Freeze full source-matched handbook/atlas editions and commit all candidate inputs.
- [ ] Build Setup/Portable from that clean commit using existing offline runtime/compiler.
- [ ] Verify exact payload/archive inventories, native dependencies, generated PCM and clean exits.
- [ ] Exercise exact packaged synthetic UI, launcher checks and isolated installer lifecycle.
- [ ] Attach exact committed PDFs and verify checksums; keep prior releases immutable.
- [ ] Publish the new tagged public prerelease and verify all five downloadable assets.
- [ ] Record exact publication/qualification evidence, finish maintained documentation and push main.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] New assets contain workstream63's repair and match their clean source/tag identity.
- [ ] Existing application/provider settings are not reset; no real recording, login or model call
  is needed merely to package the already-exercised fix.
- [ ] Synthetic/current-host evidence is separate from clean-VM, genuine old-binary migration,
  owner comfort, real-meeting recognition and recipient-capture qualification.
- [ ] Preview1/2 tags and assets are unchanged; published books match the exact packaged commit.
- [ ] No automatic fallback or relaxed safety contract is introduced by release packaging.

## Evidence

- Workstream63 passed Core809, synthetic WPF and bounded current-Agency synthetic inference.
  Six older/current/future-compatible scripted cases passed again during the later confirmation.
- The reported HTTP400 was confirmed by the owner to be in this coding chat, not Phantom Fudge;
  it is not evidence of an app HTTP defect or an observed server-side repair.
- Packaging/publication gates for this candidate are pending, not inherited from Preview2.
- Candidate preparation passed Core809, runtime-bundle19 and installed-runtime18 tests,
  Docs21 and Site14. The existing range-capable site server passed all nine browser groups.
- Full397-page handbook and709-page source atlas were generated and representative new version,
  installation, website and source annotation pages reviewed. No real audio or provider call
  was made during this release preparation. The earlier provider smoke belongs to workstream63.

